# Architecture

## Directory Structure

Feature-based structure: business logic lives in `features/`, reusable primitives live in `ui/`, and routes stay thin in `app/`.

src/
├── app/                  # Next.js App Router routes and layouts
│   ├── (marketing)/      # grouped marketing routes
│   ├── (account)/        # grouped account routes
│   ├── api/              # API routes (RESTful)
│   └── layout.tsx
├── features/             # business-logic components
│   ├── [feature]/        # flat feature files/folders, no subfolder barrels
│   ├── index.ts          # client-safe public API
│   └── server.ts         # server-only public API
├── ui/                   # reusable UI primitives and wrappers
│   ├── shadcn/           # raw shadcn primitives (internal only)
│   ├── icons/            # icon definitions
│   ├── providers/        # theme and font providers
│   └── index.ts          # public UI barrel
├── alerts/               # user feedback system
├── config/               # metadata, mocks, constants
├── lib/                  # auth, db, email, swagger, validations
├── stores/               # Effector stores
├── utils/                # pure utilities, no side effects
└── types/                # shared TypeScript types

## Key Patterns

- Thin route files in `src/app/**/page.tsx`: import + re-export only
- Business logic in `src/features/` and server-only exports in `src/features/server.ts`
- Reusable UI accessed through `@/ui`, never `@/ui/shadcn/*`
- Database queries via `src/lib/db/` (Kysely)
- Route protection and request-level auth checks use `src/proxy.ts`
- Shared types are defined once in types/ and imported everywhere
